Using $B$ meson data collected by the LHCb experiment at a center-of-mass energy of 7 TeV, corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 3 fb$^{-1}$, this study presents the first direct measurement of the differential decay rate form for $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$. This analysis relies on 1.2 fb$^{-1}$ of data. By reconstructing the final state $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ via the cascade $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ and $D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$, researchers leveraged the properties of the neutrino to infer decay dynamics. The resulting form factor exhibits a smooth behavior, with the slope parameter $f_L$ determined to be $0.25\pm0.08\pm0.04$, where the first uncertainty stems from statistical variation and the second from systematic sources.
